-- mod-fly-in-old-world (Tofu Worldview fork): make every Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor area flyable on the server.
-- Changes: areatable_dbc gets the full stock record of each of the 972 AreaTable.dbc records with ContinentID 0 or 1 (Eastern Kingdoms 499, Kalimdor 473), with Flags |= 0x400 (AREA_FLAG_OUTLAND, the flag AreaTableEntry::IsFlyable checks). Nothing else changes, except Tofu Worldview sanctuary areas 876, which also get Flags |= 0x800 (AREA_FLAG_SANCTUARY: no PvP attacks, duels still allowed). Whether a character may actually fly there is decided by the module (FlyInOldWorld.* in mod_fly_in_old_world.conf).
-- Schema: acore_world. A DB row replaces the whole DBC record with the same ID, so each row carries the full record.
-- Generated by tools/gen_areatable.py from the server stock AreaTable.dbc, sha1 8c7ced99f8dddd48296551efe05a2cf27b26f818. Re-runnable: DELETE by ID list, then INSERT fixed values.
-- Needs: worldserver restart (DBC stores load at startup). Clients need the matching AreaTable.dbc in patch-z.mpq, or they refuse to take off.
-- Check: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM acore_world.areatable_dbc WHERE ContinentID IN (0, 1) AND (Flags & 1024) <> 0; -- expected 972
-- Check: SELECT ID, Flags FROM acore_world.areatable_dbc WHERE (Flags & 2048) <> 0; -- expected 876, 3136; 4281, 1086856491
-- Revert: revert/revert_tofu_fiow_01_areatable_flyable.sql

